          "description": "Newly recorded in Prince Edward Island: scattered distribution in the Maritime Provinces (Fig. 1). Found in Alaska and in Canada from the Yukon and British Columbia east to Newfoundland and Nova Scotia (Campbell 1991 c). Transcontinental in areas of boreal forest. Larvae live in sapwood or red­rotten conifer logs (Pollock 2002 c).",
